      "body": "## Motivation\n\nUngrouped routing without a correction bias always enters the NPU softmax fast path, even when `scoring_func=\"sigmoid\"`. That path also omits `routed_scaling_factor` when `apply_routed_scaling_factor_on_output=True`.\n\nFor logits whose leading entries are `[0, 1, 2]` (remaining experts at -20), top-2 normalized sigmoid weights should be approximately `[0.546449, 0.453551]`; the current path returns `[0.731059, 0.268941]`. With normalized softmax and an enabled scale of 2.5, the current weights sum to 1 instead of 2.5.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Restrict the softmax fast path to softmax scoring and apply the requested output scale after conversion to FP32.\n- Route normalized sigmoid through the existing generic NPU fused operation.\n- Use the shared native TopK helper for unbiased, ungrouped sigmoid with `renormalize=False`, preserving FP32 weights, int32 IDs, and NPU finalization. The generic NPU operation normalizes sigmoid scores even with `renorm=False`, so changing the fast-path condition alone is insufficient.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nExecuted a separate validation script on Ascend 910C with real NPU operators and the full Python source tree; only recorder/capture and expert-placement global state are mocked. The independent reference computes FP32 scores and checks selected IDs, weights, output dtypes, padded-row zeroing and recorder masking.\n\n| Source | Passing subcases | Failing subcases |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Before | 84 | 108 |\n| After | 192 | 0 |\n\nEnvironment: PyTorch 2.10.0+cpu, torch_npu 2.10.0.post6, sgl-kernel-npu 2026.9.0 (older than the current Docker pin 2026.9.0.post12). The tested `topk.py` hash matches the source in this PR. The validation script is retained separately and is not included in the PR diff. Tested base: `1f834c19`; the relevant TopK code is unchanged in main `a4a6eddd`.\n\nCoverage: softmax/sigmoid, normalization on/off, scaling on/off, FP32/FP16/BF16, token counts 1/4, top-k 2/4, and padded/unpadded batches.\n\n### Test results screenshot\n\nThe screenshot below renders the saved hardware-test results; it is not a new test run or a GitHub CI result. [Raw results and source hashes](https://github.com/AkiYangDev/sglang/blob/2f70a5a06e47dcc0dc1f5e880c8919cbfdf1600d/RESULT.json).\n\n![Ascend 910C TopK validation: before 84 passed / 108 failed; after 192 passed / 0 failed](https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/AkiYangDev/sglang@2f70a5a06e47dcc0dc1f5e880c8919cbfdf1600d/validation-report.png)\n\nFormatting/lint checks passed. Three repository hooks requiring the `python3` executable were run separately with the available Python interpreter on Windows and passed. No model-level accuracy evaluation was run.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNo performance claim or serving benchmark. The existing softmax kernel remains in use, with a multiplication only when output scaling is enabled. Normalized sigmoid uses the existing fused kernel; unnormalized sigmoid uses the native helper for correct semantics.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format code and run applicable checks.\n- [x] Validate with a separate NPU regression script; attach recorded results.\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style.\n- [ ] Model-level accuracy and speed benchmarks (not run).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41186551196](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41186551196)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41186550967](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41186550967)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41186551070](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41186551070)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
